cff-version: 1.2.0
title: ZMO Visualisations
message: >-
  If you use these visualisations, or the data behind them, please cite the
  repository as below.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Madore
    given-names: Frédérick
    orcid: https://orcid.org/0000-0003-0959-2092
    affiliation: University of Bayreuth
abstract: >-
  Two static web apps built from data scraped from the Leibniz-Zentrum Moderner
  Orient (ZMO) website: an interactive word cloud of the most frequent terms in
  each research unit's description and project abstracts, and a cross-filtering
  dashboard of ZMO's publication register — output per year, document types,
  authors, co-authorship, journals and publishers. Both are published in English
  and German, and both are rebuilt monthly from zmo.de by Python pipelines run
  from GitHub Actions.
repository-code: https://github.com/ZMO-Berlin/visualisations
url: https://zmo-berlin.github.io/visualisations/
# Split, and both are listed because the repository ships both: MIT for the
# code, CC BY 4.0 for the scraped datasets. See LICENSE and LICENSE-DATA.
license:
  - MIT
  - CC-BY-4.0
keywords:
  - data visualisation
  - digital humanities
  - word cloud
  - bibliometrics
  - publication register
  - research data
  - web scraping
  - Leibniz-Zentrum Moderner Orient
# The site is rebuilt monthly rather than released in versions. Bump this when
# tagging a release; add `version:` and `doi:` at the same time if the tag is
# archived to Zenodo.
date-released: '2026-08-05'
references:
  - type: database
    title: ZMO publication register
    abstract: >-
      The source of the publications dashboard, and of the research-unit and
      project text behind the word cloud.
    authors:
      - name: Leibniz-Zentrum Moderner Orient
        city: Berlin
        country: DE
        website: https://www.zmo.de/
    url: https://www.zmo.de/en/publications/publication-search
